WEBVTT

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:19.000
The world’s biggest and greatest
Pokémon Battle fest to decide the world’s best...

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.710
...is finally here.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:26.260
That is... The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.890
Satoshi and Pikachu have arrived
at the place these fateful battles will be held.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.640
There he is!

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.020
You’re Satoshi from Kanto, right?

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.770
Huh? Yeah, why?

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:42.360
I request a battle from you!
Right here and now!

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.730
C’mon, battle me!

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.820
Do you think he knows
you’re one of the Masters Eight?

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.320
I can hear you.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.000
Of course I already knew that.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.250
I’m going to test your strength!

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:02.880
Sure, you’re on!
Sell me on a battle and you <i>know</i> I'm buying!

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.130
It’s go time, Pikachu!

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.600
Wooloo! Sheep Pokémon!
Normal type!

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:50.320
Its curly fleece
is a very effective cushion!

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.610
It could fall off a cliff
and be just fine!

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:56.030
Wooloo, huh?
It probably has good defenses.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.240
Move in, Wooloo!
Use Double Kick!

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.330
Iron Tail!

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.380
Wooloo!

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.670
Huh?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:14.880
That was it?

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.090
That attack...
You really <i>are</i> strong!

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.390
I see why my bro
has his eyes on you!

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:21.970
Huh? Your bro?

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.350
Yeah! I’m Hop!

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.560
Dande’s little brother!

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:27.980
Mr. Dande’s?!

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.310
Little brother?!

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:32.230
Mr. Dande talks about me?!

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.280
Don’t know why,
but that makes me so happy!

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.780
But let me warn you!

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.580
I’ll be the one
to take down my bro!

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.740
Until then,
he’ll never lose to anyone!

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.960
Okay, we’re on!

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.580
<i>Wha-bam Z!</i>

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.460
As always, your hosts are
Princess Number Thirteen!

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.630
Dolled-up Blue-bruise!

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.760
And Charm Head Deluxe, meow!

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.890
Today, we’re not in the studio, but broadcasting live
from the Pokémon World Championships!

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:01.890
Look at all this!
Everyone’s super excited!

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.810
Shoot Stadium
is packed full of crowds!

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:08.520
You just know it’s a festival
with tons of strong Pokémon, meow!

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.360
We’ll be showcasing them
one after another, so stay tuned!

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.400
...and “showcasing them”
is our cover story, meow.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.410
We can’t pass up
so many strong Pokémon.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:22.700
We’ll catch them all
in one fell swoop!

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:30.790
Cutting it close, Satoshi!

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.710
Oh! Iris!

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.960
We both made it
to the Masters Eight!

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.920
Yeah! I’ve been looking forward
to seeing you today!

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.930
Same here!
I’ve made it this far...

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:42.430
I’m gonna win!

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:52.730
Now, Shoot Stadium
is crammed full with spectators.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:57.070
You can already hear cheers
in anticipation of the heated battles.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.030
Hey!

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:03.410
Hi.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.700
Can I sit with you?
We could watch together!

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.830
Yeah, that’s fine!

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:08.790
I’m Go.
Nice to meet you.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.420
Yeah! Let’s make some noise!

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:16.710
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.670
The biggest tournament in history,

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:25.430
where the highest-ranked eight, the Masters Eight,
determine the greatest Pokémon battler.

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:29.180
And so, which of them
will be crowned...

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.190
...Championships Monarch?!

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.810
Now, let’s introduce the Masters Eight.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.940
First, ranked eighth...

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.740
The shining first Champion
of the Alola Region’s first-ever League.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:44.950
Hailing from Masara Town in Kanto,
Competitor Satoshi!

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.950
All right!
Let’s do this!

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.710
Satoshi!

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:52.580
Ranked seventh...

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:54.330
Aiming to be a Dragon Master,

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:58.250
and still growing ever stronger.
The young Champion of Isshu,

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.460
Competitor Iris!

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:02.930
Iris!

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:04.720
I’m cheering for you, too!

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.050
Wait, you know Iris too?

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.930
Everyone! Thank you!

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:14.560
Ranked sixth...

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.270
An adventurer renowned
for excavating Mega Stones.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.820
The winner of the Kalos League
Miare Tournament,

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:22.240
Competitor Alan!

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.500
Ranked fifth...

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:34.040
A world-renowned actress
enters the stage.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:37.130
Just as skilled in battle as on camera,
she is the Champion of Kalos,

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:39.340
Competitor Carne!

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.170
Ranked fourth...

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.180
The New Champion
of Kanto and Johto.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.640
One of the Pokémon G-Men
fighting evil far and near.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:50.640
Competitor Wataru!

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.350
Ranked third...

00:06:55.350 --> 00:07:00.320
The heir to Hoenn’s Devon Corporation
and Champion of Hoenn,

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.070
Competitor Daigo!

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:07.110
Ranked second...

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:11.240
The authority on Pokémon archaeology
and Champion of Sinnoh,

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.870
Competitor Shirona!

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.840
And ranked first...

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:27.590
The Champion of Galar, and the reigning Monarch of the Pokémon World Championships,

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:31.720
The world’s strongest...
The unbeaten...

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.850
Competitor Dande!

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.860
Big Bro!

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.620
I’m so happy
to see this in person!

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:58.000
What a miraculous moment, to see these eight,
Champions from far and wide, gathered in one place.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:02.130
This is the true thrill
of the Pokémon World Championships.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:07.840
In the Masters Tournament, even the undefeated Monarch, Competitor Champion Dande,

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:12.600
will be starting from the first round,
on equal footing with the other seven here.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.770
Competitor Dande,
could you give us a few words!

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.140
Bring it on!

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:20.150
Me and my Pokémon
will take down all comers!

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:32.030
And with that, it’s time to announce
the match-ups for the first round.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.670
The first match:
Competitor Dande VS Competitor Alan!

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.800
Alan’s up against Mr. Dande...

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:54.810
The second match:
Competitor Wataru VS Competitor Carne!

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:04.820
The third match:
Competitor Shirona VS Competitor Iris!

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:08.070
Ahh, it’s Ms. Shirona...

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:09.530
Go easy on me, okay?

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:11.610
The fourth match...

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:16.540
Competitor Daigo VS Competitor Satoshi!

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:18.700
My first opponent is...

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:20.790
...Mr. Daigo.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.790
So I finally get a chance
to battle you.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:31.550
Those will be the match-ups
for the Masters Eight’s first round.

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.010
Man, doesn’t this
get you pumped up?!

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:36.560
Pumped, pumped!

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:39.930
I can’t wait to see
what Pokémon they’ll use, meow!

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:46.480
Where’s Satoshi?

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.940
Oh, Satoshi said
he’d watch it with Go.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.910
He said he wanted to feel
the heat of the stadium up close.

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:55.620
That’s just like Satoshi.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:58.040
You’re not going to join him?

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:02.460
Oh, um... Actually, I had something
I wanted to ask you two...

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:06.090
Could I take a photo with you?!

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:07.630
So that’s it.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:09.210
Of course!

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:13.260
It sounds like
you know that Alan well.

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:15.390
As the stones guide me.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:21.230
Yet, to face Dande right away...
I hope he doesn’t get overwhelmed.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.230
Okay, say cheese!

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:32.360
Now, the first match of the first round...
The competitors are entering the stadium.

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:49.040
Watching from the stands is the best!

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.710
Yeah!

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:55.970
Competitor Alan even works as
an assistant to Kalos’s Professor Platane.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:00.470
I bet that the Professor
will be watching this battle from Kalos.

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:06.650
The regulations today: you may each use
three Pokémon in the first round!

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:10.980
There is no limit on match length
or switching out Pokémon.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:16.160
Whoever makes all three of their opponent’s Pokémon
unable to battle will be the winner.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:23.120
Additionally, you are allowed a single use of only one
of the following: Daimax, a Z-Move, or Mega Evolution.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.540
Now then, both battlers,
send your first Pokémon out onto the field!

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:27.540
Three!

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:28.540
Two!

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:29.540
One!

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:30.790
Go!

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:33.010
Come out, Gorillander!

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:33.010
Come out, Brigarron!

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:13.210
Brigarron! Spiny Armor Pokémon!
Grass/Fighting type!

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:16.720
When it takes a defensive posture
with its fists guarding its face,

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:19.640
it can withstand any impact!

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:22.300
So it’s a battle between Grass types...

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:27.600
Everyone watching the stream...
The battles are finally starting, meow!

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:31.270
That trainer with the fluffy neck thing...
I’ve seen him somewhere before.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:31.900
The first match in the first round is a showdown between Dande and Alan, meow!

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:34.230
Better check out his Pokémon, too...

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:38.570
Let the battle begin!

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:41.780
Now, it’s Champion Time!

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:44.450
Arm Hammer!

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:51.670
A fierce Arm Hammer!

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:54.920
But Gorillander endures it!

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.300
What?!

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:57.300
Already?!

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:58.550
Now that’s what I want to see!

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:08.520
Kyodai... max!

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:19.150
Here it is!
Competitor Dande’s Kyodaimax!

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.410
I’m not a drum!

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:29.040
Come on,
follow my bro’s beat!

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.550
Brigarron!
Brace for attack!

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:46.060
It’s one of the duties of a Champion
to get the crowd fired up!

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:47.930
Kyodai Drum Bash!

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:54.440
Needle Guard!

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:02.450
Even Needle Guard won’t be enough
to completely block Daimax attacks.

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:05.820
But I can withstand them.
That’s what Brigarron is here for!

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.330
How about this one, then?

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:09.370
Dai Jet!

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:16.500
Gyro Ball!

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:25.720
Brigarron shrugs off the Dai Jet...

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.930
...and hits with Gyro Ball!

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:30.890
All right!

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:32.310
That was good.

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:34.020
Amazing!

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:36.190
He’s doing well,
considering his opponent.

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:38.020
He mustn’t let his guard down.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:41.440
Dai Jet will have raised
Gorillander’s speed.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:42.690
Needle Missile!

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:46.320
Dai Earth!

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:56.710
And that’s the end
for Gorillander’s Kyodaimax!

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:57.710
Gyro Ball!

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:58.710
Acrobat!

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:08.100
Brigarron!

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:12.310
A magnificent Acrobat!
His aerial attack landed!

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:16.270
Brigarron is unable to battle!

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:19.480
Competitor Alan
has lost his first Pokémon!

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.400
Good job, Big Bro!

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:24.320
Mr. Dande beat him at
Grass against Grass, huh?

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:26.490
That was an incredibly fast attack...

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:29.490
So Dande was a step ahead.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:32.580
Yes. For it to know Acrobat...

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:41.250
You did well. Take a rest.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:42.880
Come out, Lizardon!

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.930
His second Pokémon is Lizardon!

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:53.720
We’ve battled Alan’s Lizardon
lots of times before.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:55.140
Huh...

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:00.150
You’ve got a good glare.

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:02.820
I’ll make you show me
how strong you are.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:05.150
Drum Attack!

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:10.530
Flare Drive!

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:23.250
It’s super effective!

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.460
Gorillander is unable to battle!

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.800
Lizardon takes down Gorillander!

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.930
Now they’re even!

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.640
Good work, Lizardon!

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:37.230
Bro...

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:39.850
Well, well...
It’s not looking so sure now...

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:40.810
Yeah!

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:45.150
Gorillander... That was marvelous.
You’re strong!

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:47.570
My second Pokémon...

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:48.570
Come out!

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:54.080
That’s it! My bro’s ace!

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:59.830
Competitor Dande’s strongest partner,
Lizardon, has arrived!

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:01.960
Dragon Claw!

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:03.340
Air Slash!

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:10.300
So, I can’t get close enough...
Well, in that case...

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:12.470
Return, Lizardon!

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:16.390
Oh, Competitor Alan
is switching Pokémon!

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:18.770
Come out, Calamanero!

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:23.940
Your powers will turn
the tide of the battle!

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:26.940
Competitor Alan’s third Pokémon
is Calamanero.

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:32.570
Calamanero! Turnaround Pokémon!
Evil/Psychic type!

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:36.990
Gazing at its luminescent spots
will quickly induce a hypnotic state,

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.960
putting the observer
under Calamanero’s control!

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:41.790
Psycho Cutter!

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:44.670
Great Blaze!

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:50.920
Rush in! Use Hell Thrust!

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:52.880
Air Slash!

00:17:58.720 --> 00:17:59.730
Great Blaze!

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:11.240
Calamanero is unable to battle!

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:14.700
Competitor Alan
has lost his second Pokémon!

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:19.450
I couldn’t give you
a chance to shine. I’m sorry.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:22.120
He’s strong...

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:25.130
The pendulum’s swung
all the way in Mr. Dande’s favor.

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:27.790
Head forth, Lizardon!

00:18:28.590 --> 00:18:31.170
I will keep going with Lizardon!

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:35.680
It was my dream
to battle against your Lizardon.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.680
And to surpass it!

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:43.560
Heed my heart’s call,
Key Stone!

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.650
Transcend evolution...

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:48.070
Mega Evolve!

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:16.970
Yes! Mega Lizardon X!

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:18.470
Dragon Claw!

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.060
Ancient Power!

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:38.410
Flare Drive!

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.910
Dragon Pulse!

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:54.760
Dragon Pulse is super effective!

00:19:57.090 --> 00:20:02.260
Competitor Alan’s Lizardon is unable to battle!
Competitor Dande’s Lizardon wins!

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:06.020
As such, the winner is
Competitor Dande!

00:20:12.320 --> 00:20:14.990
The first match
of the first round has concluded.

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:18.660
Competitor Dande
advances to the semifinals!

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:21.830
That was an awesome battle!

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:24.040
Mr. Dande’s so strong...

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:26.660
Big Bro! Lizardon!

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:32.960
Competitor Alan was forced into a tough battle
by Competitor Dande’s skillful attacks,

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:35.550
but he put up a great fight!

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:38.010
You fought well.

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:42.640
Hey! Hey!
Wasn’t that battle amazing?!

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:44.680
Look forward to the next match!

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:45.810
The second match is—

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:50.940
I’m tired.
Break time.

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:52.690
Don’t fall asleep, meow!

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:54.730
Keep working! Work!

00:20:55.570 --> 00:20:56.940
This is hopeless.

00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:04.450
I’ll retrain myself,
and then I’ll be back.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:06.700
Right. I’ll be waiting!

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:13.000
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament...

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.460
...has begun with a victory for Dande.

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:18.260
And the next match is between...

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:19.840
Now, then...

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:22.340
Please, don’t hold back
on my account.

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:24.600
I would ask the same.

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:31.100
...the Dragon Tamer Wataru,
known throughout Kanto and Johto...

00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:34.360
...and the Champion of Kalos, Carne.

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:36.980
Whoever wins battles Mr. Dande!

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:38.240
Yeah!

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:42.280
Which of the two will emerge victorious in the
second match?

00:23:06.410 --> 00:23:10.870
Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament News!

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:14.870
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament!

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:16.080
It’s the best, meow!

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:18.960
The second match is between
Competitors Wataru and Carhrhrhr!

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:19.710
What did you just say?

00:23:19.710 --> 00:23:20.670
Competitor Carhrhrhr!

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:22.460
That’s the star actress,
Carne, meow!

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:24.130
Humph! Never heard of her!

00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:27.300
Guess she’ll just have to show us
how a “star actress” battles, then!

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:29.430
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:29.430 --> 00:23:32.180
The Champions’ Pride!
Wataru VS Carne!!

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:34.100
Let’s all tune in, meow!
